{
  "abstract": "Pure-kernel Lean 4 formalization resolving the two-qubit (n = 2) maximal magic conjecture of Liu, Low, and Yin (Quantum Sci. Technol. 11, 015035, 2026; Open Quantum Problem E28) for all Stabilizer Rényi Entropy (SRE) orders α ≥ 2. Using the SU(4) ≅ Spin(6) reduction onto the positively oriented skew-orthogonal manifold in SO(6) and an exact degree-8 B₆⁺-equivariant rational sum-of-squares certificate verified by definitional equality inside Lean's kernel, the formalization proves the sharp upper bound M_α(|ψ⟩) ≤ (1/(1-α)) log((1 + 3·4^(1-α))/4) (in particular max M_2 = log(16/7)), proves attainment by |ψ_MUB⟩ = (1/2)(1, 1, 1, i), classifies all maximizers as a single two-qubit Clifford orbit of exact cardinality 480 coinciding with the two-qubit Pauli 5-MUB fiducial states, and proves the exact Wootters concurrence dichotomy C ∈ {1/2, 1/√2} with 192 / 288 state counts. AI-assistance disclosure: the bulk of the technical work (proof discovery, SOS certificate pipeline, Lean 4 formalization, and manuscript drafting) was carried out using AI systems under the author's problem selection, direction, and oversight; mathematical correctness rests on Lean 4's kernel verification and the standalone exact-integer Python certificate verifier.",
